                <pb facs="0309" n="216" xml:id="pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2483: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-23T12:00:00-05:00">July 23,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Yesterday afternoon the Minister for Foreign Affairs submitted the Bio de
                    Janeiro protocol to the Senate with a lengthy message recommending its
                    ratification. A bill approving the protocol was passed unanimously in first
                    reading which is wholly perfunctory and was then referred to Foreign Relations
                    Committee for report within 15 days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
